What it covers

  The result and protocol files published in site/public/data/ — served at
  https://bci.report/data/ and listed with the SHA-256 of each file at
  https://bci.report/releases/ — the copies of the same exports the pages are
  built from in site/src/data/ (mvp.json is experiments.json), and the same
  tables on the Hugging Face mirror
  https://huggingface.co/datasets/Twu31/bci-report. These are cohort-level
  measurements computed by BCI Report: scores, intervals, cohort sizes and the
  protocol descriptors that produced them.

What it does not cover

  The EEG recordings the measurements were computed from. They are not in this
  repository, they belong to the people who collected them, and they keep their
  own licences and terms. Every result row and every dataset page names its
  source and that source's licence: https://bci.report/datasets/

  The code. It is under the MIT License (see LICENSE).

How to give credit

  Name "BCI Report", the release you used (its id is on
  https://bci.report/releases/) and https://bci.report, and cite the upstream
  dataset each figure was computed on. CITATION.cff holds the same citation in
  machine-readable form.
